  "scope": "A pinned CNCF Distribution registry in the supervisor cluster is the source; two separately addressed pinned Distribution registries in the disposable owned-peer Kind cluster are the only candidate destinations. The exact source-to-unapproved-destination pair and one fixed tag are first copied without governance, then removed and refused by the governed path. The approved destination path is also exercised. Membership is a real ConfigMap managed by a least-privilege service account; a separate observer independently checks that resource and each registry manifest. Reconciliation is capped at four API read/repair passes. The scratch extension selects one new immutable approval snapshot, observes one native CronJob reconciliation invocation, and verifies refusal of the formerly approved pair; this is not evidence of sustained schedule reliability or production endpoint identity.",
